              "value": "Photograph of the Tollinton Market building under-construction, Lahore, Punjab, 1863. The building was originally built for the 1864 Punjab Exhibition of Arts and Industry. Originally the Punjab Exhibition Hall, this building later became known as Tollinton Market. It was also referred to as the \"Ajaib Ghar\" (\"House of Wonders\"). \n<p>\"A building was erected at Anarkullee, Lahore, from local, provincial and imperial funds, for the Punjab Exhibition of natural products, arts and manufacturers which was opened on 20th January 1864, and closed in the first week of April. the building is now to be used, one wing for the Lahore museum, and the other for public meetings and general purposes.\" \u2013\u2013 Annual report of the Public Works Department (Buildings and Roads) for 1863-64\n</p><p>Another source claims this photograph was taken in 1893: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.the-south-asian.com/March-April2006/Tollinton_Market_1.htm\">[1]</a> (Courtesy of the Calendar Lahore Conservation Society)\n</p>\nFurther info/images: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/p/1FPb4TT6kX/\">[2]</a>; <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/share/p/15S7Vka29TA/\">[3]</a>",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
